Follow-up to #84, in a region that fix did not cover.

karr push now reads Git::Native::Remote::Result and fails on a non-empty
->rejected with the per-ref reason, and SyncLifecycle no longer retries a
rejection -- one attempt, one report, because the server already answered.

App::karr::SyncGuard has its own push path (the insurance push drained from the
END block, see #37) and it did not get the same treatment: it still makes three
attempts at a push the server has already declined, and ends with the generic
"Local refs are intact. Run karr sync to push them." advice regardless of why
the push failed.

So the one path that runs when a command has already died is also the one that
reports the least. Work: consume the same rejection contract in SyncGuard, do
not retry a rejection, and say what the remote refused rather than advising a
retry that will fail identically.
Fixed and merged into main (fa79722); full suite green at 93 files / 630 tests.
Reproduced before the fix, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix
code. #94 additionally confirmed empirically that libgit2 lookup-based delete
really does guard: moving the ref underneath it answers "old reference value
does not match".
